      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/id": "89e0ec45-c6c5-510c-8d5d-815a56ed5603",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ for the variables $x,y,z$ in that order.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system. Select the solution $(x,y,z)$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_2:=R_2+(1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$R_3:=R_3+(-1)R_1$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThe second pivot is zero, while the third row has a nonzero second entry. Exchange $R_2$ and $R_3$.\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nThus the row echelon matrix is\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nBack substitute, starting with the last row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z &=1 \\\\ y &=0-(1)(1) \\\\ &=-1 \\\\ x &=-3-(-2)(-1) \\\\ &\\quad -(-1)(1) \\\\ &=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution $(x,y,z)$ is\n\n$$\n\\left(-4,-1,1\\right)\n$$\n\n"
    }
